import OAI.Combinatorics.HoneycombChords.BridgeLaplace

/-!
# Critical honeycomb bridge mass

For simple honeycomb paths weighted by the critical activity per visited center,
the strict bridge mass at height `h` is comparable to `(1 + h)^(-1/4)`, with
height-zero mass equal to one. Its height Laplace transform is comparable to
`s^(-3/4)` for `0 < s ≤ 1`.

The geometric port convention and finite strip transfer estimates follow OpenAI,
*Critical honeycomb chords with prescribed boundary endpoints* and its companion
*Uniform marked-polygon estimates and sharp finite bridge moments* (September 26, 2026).
-/
